---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Ship a new rule: straight to production, or in shadow mode first" hint="A candidate rule blocks payments that the current rules let through. Change the rule and the rollout, and see how many good customers it hurts and what the shadow report would have said.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start as it is: <b>straight to everyone</b>, blocking any card with <b>2 or more payments in a minute</b>, with <b>any amount</b>. It stops 98 more frauds but blocks 2,128 good payments, so the day ends <b>$56,583 down</b>. Nobody saw it coming.</li>
    <li>Switch the rollout to <b>shadow mode first</b>: the same rule is only recorded. The report shows it would lose money, so it is held back, <b>0 customers</b> are affected and the result is <b>$0</b>.</li>
    <li>Raise the amount floor to <b>$200</b> with 2 payments: the rule is much sharper and the shadow report promotes it, for <b>+$16,807</b>.</li>
    <li>Use <b>3 payments</b> with a floor of <b>$200</b> in shadow mode: after <b>1 or 7 days</b> only 10% or 40% of the frauds have a label yet, so a good rule (+$5,016) looks bad and is held back. After <b>30 days</b> it is promoted.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg frb" data-frb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Block when the card has at least this many payments in a minute <input type="range" min="1" max="4" value="2" data-n /> <b data-nval></b></label>
      <label>and the amount is at least <select class="pg-in" data-floor>
        <option value="0" selected>any amount</option>
        <option value="100">$100</option>
        <option value="200">$200</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Rollout <select class="pg-in" data-mode>
        <option value="live" selected>straight to everyone</option>
        <option value="shadow">shadow mode first, then promote if the report is positive</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Shadow report after <select class="pg-in" data-days>
        <option value="1">1 day</option>
        <option value="7" selected>7 days</option>
        <option value="30">30 days</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Cost of blocking a good payment (dollars) <input type="range" min="10" max="100" step="10" value="40" data-fp /> <b data-fpval></b></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Good payments blocked</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Fraud newly stopped</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Shadow report</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Net result for the day</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: 20,000 payments in a day, of which 249 are fraud (1.2%, much higher than real life so the effect is visible). Busy but honest cards often make several payments in a minute. The current rules already block 104 frauds with 4 or more payments and an amount of $100 or more, and the candidate counts only what that rule lets through. A stopped fraud saves its amount plus a $15 chargeback fee. The shadow report counts only frauds that have a label by then, which is 10% after 1 day, 40% after 7 days and 80% after 30 days, and it promotes the rule if the labelled savings are higher than the cost of the good payments it would block.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-frb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const PAYMENTS = 20000;
    let seed = 11; const rnd = (n: number) => { seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296; return Math.floor(seed / 65536) % n; };
    type P = { fraud: boolean; c: number; amt: number };
    const pop: P[] = [];
    for (let i = 0; i < PAYMENTS; i++) {
      const fraud = rnd(1000) < 12;
      if (fraud) pop.push({ fraud, c: 1 + rnd(5), amt: 80 + rnd(420) }), rnd(100);
      else if (rnd(100) < 8) pop.push({ fraud, c: rnd(5), amt: 20 + rnd(250) }), rnd(100);
      else pop.push({ fraud, c: rnd(100) < 85 ? 0 : 1 + rnd(2), amt: 5 + rnd(120) }), rnd(100);
    }
    const KNOWN: Record<string, number> = { '1': 0.1, '7': 0.4, '30': 0.8 };
    const money = (n: number) => `${n < 0 ? '-' : n > 0 ? '+' : ''}$${Math.abs(Math.round(n)).toLocaleString('en-US')}`;
    const num = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
    function simulate(n: number, floor: number, fp: number, share: number) {
      let stopped = 0; let saved = 0; let good = 0;
      for (const p of pop) {
        if (p.c >= 4 && p.amt >= 100) continue; // already blocked by the current rules
        if (p.c < n || p.amt < floor) continue;
        if (p.fraud) { stopped++; saved += p.amt + 15; } else good++;
      }
      const lost = good * fp; const net = saved - lost; const est = saved * share - lost;
      return { stopped, saved, good, lost, net, est };
    }
    function draw() {
      const n = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-n]').value); const floor = Number(q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-floor]').value);
      const mode = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-mode]').value; const days = q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-days]').value;
      const fp = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fp]').value);
      q('[data-nval]').textContent = String(n); q('[data-fpval]').textContent = `$${fp}`;
      q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-days]').disabled = mode === 'live';
      const share = KNOWN[days]; const r = simulate(n, floor, fp, share);
      const shadow = mode === 'shadow'; const promoted = !shadow || r.est > 0;
      const good = promoted ? r.good : 0; const stopped = promoted ? r.stopped : 0; const result = promoted ? r.net : 0;
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = num(good);
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = shadow ? (promoted ? `none during the test, ${num(r.good)} after promotion` : 'none, the rule never went live') : `costing ${money(-r.lost)}`;
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = num(stopped);
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = promoted ? `saving ${money(r.saved)}` : `it would have stopped ${num(r.stopped)}`;
      if (shadow) {
        q('[data-o3]').textContent = `${promoted ? 'promote' : 'hold back'} (${money(r.est)})`;
        q('[data-n3]').textContent = `${num(Math.round(r.stopped * share))} of ${num(r.stopped)} frauds labelled after ${days} day${days === '1' ? '' : 's'}, against ${num(r.good)} good payments that would be blocked`;
      } else {
        q('[data-o3]').textContent = 'none';
        q('[data-n3]').textContent = 'the rule goes live for everyone at once';
      }
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = money(result);
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = promoted ? `true value of the rule: ${money(r.net)} per day` : `the rule would have given ${money(r.net)} per day`;
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b1]').style.setProperty('--c', good > 0 && r.lost > r.saved ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--accent)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b2]').style.setProperty('--c', 'var(--accent)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b3]').style.setProperty('--c', shadow ? (promoted ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--accent)') : 'var(--accent)');
      q<HTMLElement>('[data-b4]').style.setProperty('--c', result < 0 ? 'var(--bad)' : result > 0 ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--accent)');
      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); let msg = ''; let bad = false;
      if (!shadow) {
        bad = r.net < 0;
        msg = r.net < 0 ? `Straight to everyone, the rule blocked ${num(r.good)} good payments to stop ${num(r.stopped)} frauds, and the day ended ${money(r.net)}. It was found by complaints and the decline-rate alert, after the damage.`
          : `Straight to everyone, the rule was a good one (${money(r.net)}), but nothing proved that beforehand. A rule one step sharper might not have been.`;
      } else if (promoted) {
        msg = r.net >= 0 ? `The shadow report was positive, so the rule was promoted: ${money(r.net)} per day, with evidence first and no customers hurt during the test.`
          : `The report was positive but the rule loses ${money(r.net)} once all the labels are in. Shadow mode lowers the risk, and it only knows what the labels so far say.`;
        bad = r.net < 0;
      } else if (r.net > 0) {
        bad = true;
        msg = `Held back a rule that was worth ${money(r.net)} per day: after ${days} day${days === '1' ? '' : 's'} only ${Math.round(share * 100)}% of the frauds have a label, so it looked worse than it is. Wait longer, or use early labels from challenges and reviews.`;
      } else {
        msg = `Held back a rule that would have lost ${money(r.net)} per day, and ${num(r.good)} good payments were never blocked. This is what shadow mode is for.`;
      }
      out.classList.toggle('bad', bad); out.textContent = msg;
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw); root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
